INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('benefits-of-a-guest-facing-display-for-restaurants', 'Benefits of a Guest Facing Display', 'As the name suggests, a Guest Facing Display is a digital screen allowing patrons to instantly see their orders and confirm them. It also includes menu items and prices at many others. A guest facing display can...', '[{"type":"p","text":"As the name suggests, a Guest Facing Display is a digital screen allowing patrons to instantly see their orders and confirm them. It also includes menu items and prices at many others. A guest facing display can accurately improve the customer experience. It is because guests can see the details of their order, ultimately helping avoid confusion, mistakes, and delays."},{"type":"p","text":"Moreover, a guest facing display is a screen - either a monitor or a tablet - that allows you to display itemized orders and payment information to your customers at the point of sale. Compared to a self-ordering kiosk, the customer does not interact with any information on the guest facing display screen or press buttons. It uses visual confirmation. The fantastic technological breakthrough can also be customized to your restaurant’s specific branding. It provides customers additional information on unique features such as promotions, restaurant reward programs, new products, etc."},{"type":"p","text":"Furthermore, guest facing displays are most commonly used by limited-service restaurants. Most of them are fast, casual, and fast food venues. It is maybe because they can be displayed on the counter where the customer places and pays for their order. For example, in some states, including California, you may be required to display prices visually. So it is essential to check with local authorities and laws to determine guest facing displays’ compliance policy."},{"type":"p","text":"Below are some essential ways virtually every limited-service restaurant can benefit from a POS guest facing display system:"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Improves the Customer Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most important benefits of a point-of-sale display is the impact on the customer experience. The transparency provides to its customers is precious and significant. So it is because it assures them that they will receive exactly what they ordered and how much they’ll be paying for it, and other information can go a long way in establishing trust between your staff and your customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Avoid return/exchange"},{"type":"p","text":"It makes the customers aware of their list of orders and notice errors, and makes changes before placing them to pay. Usually, customers seek a refund or exchange for various reasons, especially. For example, individuals could be short on cash or make mistakes when selecting products. A guest facing display ensures they can review their choice of foods, thus reducing the return/exchange possibilities."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Increase customer engagement"},{"type":"p","text":"Many times, retailers put commercials on guest facing displays. They are intended to draw customers’ attention to a promotion, such as forthcoming seasonal or loyalty program deals, new menus, and special events. Even though waiting for payment is tedious, a humorous and imaginative banner may brighten clients’ moods. They’ll also remember your promotions for a more extended period."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Decrease Negative Reviews"},{"type":"p","text":"Considering the power of digital technology. It is more accessible for someone to write negative reviews online. It is customers’ way of showing their dissatisfaction with a restaurant. Miscommunication in many ways can be provided, without a guest facing display system. Online reviews can either build or break your restaurant. One negative comment will tarnish your business reputation and affect your sales."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Boost Tips"},{"type":"p","text":"Because touchscreen guest facing displays simplify for your employees to provide accurate and efficient service, your customer satisfaction levels increase, and so may the tips they leave for your employees. Plus, the touchscreen displays preset information amounts that customers can click instantly, or they can type in a custom amount right on the screen."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about eatOS'' Guest Facing Display system and enjoy exceptional features such as contactless payment, dynamic tipping, digital receipts, smartphone payments, and more."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_d80b2c7f9c3949f0aa90047615072622~mv2.jpg', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-31', 'published'),
  ('kitchen-display-system-a-key-to-running-your-restaurant', 'Kitchen Display System, a Key to Running Your Restaurant', 'The secret of successful restaurants is not only their menu, quality services, location, and ambiance. It''s probably the right kitchen display system(KDS). It''s a technology used by many to keep their menu available at...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The secret of successful restaurants is not only their menu, quality services, location, and ambiance. It''s probably the right kitchen display system(KDS). It''s a technology used by many to keep their menu available at all times, serving them to clients in the shortest time possible, proper reservation protocols to avoid the clients waiting, and a perfect venue when everything runs smoothly up to the payment method. Furthermore, the crews and managers facilitate the orders and the guests'' comfort. Finally, the back of the house, popularly known as the kitchen, is in charge of preparing the dishes in a highly-stressful environment."},{"type":"p","text":"The most challenging task is creating the best food possible to impress the customers and the intense time pressure to serve it as quickly as possible without compromising its taste and quality. The kitchen display system is a great help. It is very crucial to maintain everything in order. Delivery details, inventory, expiration dates, and even nutritional contents are some factors that keep the kitchen functioning efficiently. It has taken much work in past decades to make it perfect. Some even close their establishments to give way for inventory. But why settle for less if you can have more."},{"type":"h2","text":"Kitchen display app"},{"type":"p","text":"The role of these technological breakthroughs is primarily communication. An essential information-equipped system that will keep the operation running smoothly. These apps enable servers to key in orders displayed automatically back in the kitchen. On the other hand, all staff can monitor how many orders are coming in. This will help the kitchen know when the rush time begins in real-time. It will also allow servers to consider a long order queue and adjust customers'' expectations by serving appetizers in advance. And most importantly, these apps can signal servers to see how long customers have been waiting for their food. It will reduce potential problems such as the cancellation of orders and bad reviews online."},{"type":"h2","text":"An inventory management app"},{"type":"p","text":"It is common for every restaurant to run out of ingredients for their most popular dish during a busy hour. But now, you can manage an inventory to avoid such a disappointing scenario much less likely. A definitive list can help you monitor everything in your kitchen. It alerts you automatically when it''s time to re-order. Not only that, it helps track costs and ingredients per menu, and with inflation still on the rise, inventory management is crucial in keeping your costs under control and your profit margin."},{"type":"p","text":"We are indeed living in a digital world. Discover apps and Kitchen Display System that will run your business efficiently and automatically. At eatOs, we provide you with the latest technology for your restaurant. Talk to us now."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_725b61eb67f444828381672d64e6a70e~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-29', 'published'),
  ('self-ordering-kiosk-the-secret-weapon-for-a-successful-restaurant', 'Self-Ordering Kiosk, The Secret to a Successful Restaurant', 'The world''s famous self-ordering kiosk was first used by McDonald''s and Paneras and later became the staple technology of all fast food chains and restaurants worldwide. So if you are still not using it now, you are far...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The world''s famous self-ordering kiosk was first used by McDonald''s and Paneras and later became the staple technology of all fast food chains and restaurants worldwide. So if you are still not using it now, you are far left behind. As COVID-19 radically changed how the food industry runs its businesses, self-ordering kiosks became an essential tool to adopt the so-called new normal."},{"type":"h2","text":"Parts and functions of a Self-Ordering Kiosk"},{"type":"p","text":"1. It is built with a user-friendly algorithm that works in the background to suggest popular menu combinations based on historical data or customized customer options."},{"type":"p","text":"2. It reduces queues and waits times. Therefore, it makes customers happy and increases profitability. It helps to improve employees'' efficiency by focusing on back-of-house operations and customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"3. The innovative and simple software helps make ordering easy for all customers. It leads customers to order for themselves and save operating expenses."},{"type":"p","text":"Self-Ordering Kiosks provide an easy-to-use option for customers to order without going through long lines. It makes the ordering process fast and accurate. In restaurants, it allows guests to make their orders without the assistance of a server. Restaurants generally use hand-held tablets to do the process. It decreases the number of necessary servers, allowing restaurant staff to focus more on concerns that need to be performed manually."},{"type":"p","text":"This technological wonder is also widely used in Fast Food/QSR. It can reduce waiting time and offer faster services by sending orders directly to the kitchen. Furthermore, it decreases the risks of human error such as taking wrong orders as the guests will input their choices directly instead of the traditional ordering process."},{"type":"h2","text":"Benefits of a Self-Ordering Kiosk system"},{"type":"p","text":"1\\. It requires limited staff to assist customers."},{"type":"p","text":"2\\. More efficient customer service. More time will be allowed for customers'' other immediate concerns, such as menu inquiries or related issues."},{"type":"p","text":"3\\. It promotes social distancing. As authorities loosen COVID-19 restrictions, many customers keep the social distancing protocol and prefer a contactless transaction for efficiency and safety purposes."},{"type":"h2","text":"How do Self-Ordering Kiosk systems work"},{"type":"p","text":"The primordial objectives are to lessen labor costs, minimize waiting times and increase profitability. It should be easy to use and manage and seamlessly integrates with the point of sale and kitchen display system."},{"type":"p","text":"Here''s how to get started:"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Purchasing a kiosk"},{"type":"p","text":"The most crucial step is finding a TRUSTED KIOSK PROVIDER that fits your business. It comes in different shapes, sizes, and functions, which means the manufacturer or the provider must understand the client''s specific needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Kiosk set-up"},{"type":"p","text":"Installation is part of the job. Aside from delivery, the manufacturer or the provider must perform on-site assistance to help get the kiosk up and running perfectly. The position will not only limit the installation process but also assure that the software is properly functioning."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Using the kiosk system"},{"type":"p","text":"Once it is properly installed and fully operational, the machine begins to process orders. A user inputs their choice of foods, and it is displayed and processed through the kiosk system. In addition, It offers a wide range of ordering options and allows customers to customize their orders."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Order is automatically sent to the kitchen"},{"type":"p","text":"Customers'' orders will automatically reflect on a kitchen display system, and the kitchen personnel processes them. Imagine the amount of time saved, significantly decreasing the likelihood of incorrect orders."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Food is served"},{"type":"p","text":"The entire process is streamlined to promote convenience and efficiency to both the customer and the management. Once the order has been prepared, it is ready to be served. As a result, it provides a better customer experience that will lead them to return."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"The Self-Ordering Kiosk system is an incredible invention that provides the food industry with an enormous aid in promoting customer satisfaction and increasing profitability. Easy as it may seem, choosing the right provider is essential. Given the many positive reviews, one can''t deny that many more food establishments are adopting self-ordering kiosk systems."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_8d0637fdf1f34586bf0d124078ef8608~mv2.jpg', 'Self-Service Kiosk', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-23', 'published'),
  ('5-ways-to-bring-guests-back-to-indoor-dining', '5 Ways to Bring Guests Back to Indoor Dining', 'As restaurants get ready to reopen at full capacity this summer, they find themselves in charge of a job they’ve never had before: Convincing customers to feel ready for it, too. Sanitation, health and safety measures,...', '[{"type":"p","text":"As restaurants get ready to reopen at full capacity this summer, they find themselves in charge of a job they’ve never had before: Convincing customers to feel ready for it, too. Sanitation, health and safety measures, and keeping up with new technology will all take a lot of time and effort. Still, just doing the work isn’t enough. Your guests need to feel secure before they’re ready for indoor dining."},{"type":"p","text":"Here are five ways you can help bring your guests back to indoor dining:"},{"type":"p","text":"1\\. Keep your restaurant clean - This one is a no brainer. In order to make guests feel comfortable, your restaurant must be clean. But in today’s world, “clean” means more than just mopping the floors and taking out the trash. You need to sanitize all surfaces, including tables, chairs, doorknobs, and countertops. And don’t forget about your bathrooms!"},{"type":"p","text":"2\\. Train your staff on safety protocols - Your staff is the face of your restaurant, so it’s important that they are trained on all safety protocols. This includes things like proper handwashing, wearing masks and gloves, and sanitizing all surfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"3\\. Use technology to your advantage - There are lots of new technologies available that can help you keep your restaurant clean and safe. For example, you can use UV light to sanitize surfaces, install touchless faucets and soap dispensers, and set up a contactless ordering system."},{"type":"p","text":"4\\. Keep up with the latest guidelines - The CDC and other government agencies are constantly updating their guidelines for restaurants. Make sure you’re keeping up with the latest recommendations so you can make any necessary changes to your procedures."},{"type":"p","text":"5\\. Communicate with your guests - Finally, don’t forget to communicate with your guests! Let them know what steps you’re taking to keep them safe, and reassure them that you’re doing everything you can to create a comfortable dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"By following these tips, you can help bring your guests back to indoor dining with confidence."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_176b5793b7e14326a9b0df95a8394ce9~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-17', 'published'),
  ('could-pop-ups-be-next-for-struggling-restaurants', 'Could Pop-Ups Help Struggling Restaurants?', 'Usually, pop-ups come before the brick-and-mortar restaurant. Owners can test their concept before launching an expensive, large-scale operation. This typically makes pop-ups invaluable. So why have some restaurants...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Usually, pop-ups come before the brick-and-mortar restaurant. Owners can test their concept before launching an expensive, large-scale operation. This typically makes pop-ups invaluable. So why have some restaurants decided to turn the tables, and go backwards?"},{"type":"p","text":"The food service industry has adapted in interesting ways because of COVID-19. As the Delta variant spreads more rapidly, restaurants are once again losing customers and steady profit. It’s causing shutdowns whenever someone tests positive, and operations pause as management contact traces where possible. Nobody wants to close down again, but it’s unavoidable particularly if you don’t have the staff to cover for sick employees."},{"type":"p","text":"Even if your staff is vaccinated, news of an outbreak is still disastrous for your customers and, consequently, your reputation. Restaurants need solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Adam Gonzales on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Why Pop-Ups are Coming Back in Style"},{"type":"p","text":"When restaurants open and close every couple of months, the ideal business model does that intentionally. Build shutdown costs into the budget with a pop-up, which is designed to last a short time."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider Lord Stanley. Co-owners, chefs and partners Rupert and Carrie Blease own this San Franciscan restaurant. Now it’s transforming into Turntable at Lord Stanley. For two months apiece, they’ll host culinary names with different expertise from all around the world. The short-lived time frame works despite the spread of Delta, as the virus has less chance of doing so much damage to a business meant for a shorter time frame."},{"type":"p","text":"Limited windows have another advantage, this one less dire: It generates buzz. “while supplies last” campaigns naturally pique interest. People will talk about it, try it out, and come back again when the next pop-up comes. If you’re in the area, try it starting September 7th. Turntable at Lord Stanley will be open Tuesday through Saturday from 5:30 - 10PM."},{"type":"h2","text":"Are Pop-Ups the Solution?"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants might handle the financial strain of COVID-29 in a number of ways. Pop-ups are one viable option. Since workers don’t legally have to get vaccinated, restaurants can incentivize them with days off and provide rewards if they do it. That can help entice back workers so that your endeavors go as smoothly as possible, whether you stay a standing restaurant or try something new."},{"type":"p","text":"Find whatever fits for your restaurant, customers and capabilities. Perhaps, rather than reducing to a pop-up, you might prefer to rotate out other vendors like Lord Stanley. Partnering with local vendors puts you in the community’s good books, spreads your brand through word-of-mouth, and presents new marketing opportunities. All this helps expand your current customer base. Find clever ways to boost operations in a way that works for your restaurant. If you’re having trouble running smoothly through an old system, consider easing the transition by investing in a smarter Point of Sale."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS offers an all-in-one cloud-based eco-system exclusively for restaurants. From Point of Sale to Contactless Ordering, Pay & Order at Table, Kitchen Display System, Guest Facing Display, Online Ordering APP / Website and Workforce Management there is everything to help a restaurant succeed no matter the size. Click Here to Schedule a demo to learn more about how your restaurant can make a smooth transition into the world of restaurant technology made simple."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #PopUps #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_1c62aa5001154a12a56ae1deab20edca~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-15', 'published'),
  ('culinary-terms-from-basic-to-french', 'Culinary Terms: From Basic to French', 'There are some basic culinary terms that all chefs know and use on a regular basis. These include words like sauté, simmer, and roast. But then there are also more nuanced French culinary terms that not everyone may be...', '[{"type":"p","text":"There are some basic culinary terms that all chefs know and use on a regular basis. These include words like sauté, simmer, and roast. But then there are also more nuanced French culinary terms that not everyone may be familiar with. This blog post will define some of the most common French culinary terms and explain what they mean in the context of cooking."},{"type":"p","text":"Sauté is a French term that describes the cooking technique of frying food in a small amount of fat. This term is often used interchangeably with the word \"fry.\" Simmer, on the other hand, refers to cooking food in liquid at a low temperature so that the liquid just barely bubbles. And finally, roast means to cook food in an oven at a high temperature."},{"type":"p","text":"Now that we''ve defined some of the most common French culinary terms, let''s put them into context and see how they''re used in restaurant kitchens. Sautéing is a popular method of cooking because it''s quick and easy. Simmering is often used for soups and stews because it allows the flavors to meld together. And roasting is often used for meats and vegetables because it creates a nice, crispy exterior."},{"type":"p","text":"So there you have it! A few of the most common French culinary terms and their definitions. Bon appetit!"},{"type":"p","text":"These are just a few of the many French culinary terms that exist. While they may be some of the most common, there are still many more that chefs use on a daily basis. If you''re interested in learning more about French cuisine, consider taking a cooking class or two."},{"type":"p","text":"Or, if you''re feeling really adventurous, take a trip to France and experience it firsthand! Either way, bon appetit! restauranteurs should have a solid understanding of these words in order to create truly exquisite dining experiences for their guests."},{"type":"p","text":"After all, the restaurant business is all about creating an unforgettable experience for each and every customer. By understanding and utilizing these French culinary terms, restauranteurs can take their business to the next level. customers will be able to tell the difference between a restaurant that takes its food seriously and one that doesn''t. And in today''s competitive market, that can make all the difference."},{"type":"p","text":"Until next time, happy cooking! Or as they say in France, bon appetit! restaurants should have a solid understanding of these words in order to create truly exquisite dining experiences for their guests ."},{"type":"p","text":"Customers will be able to tell the difference between a restaurant that takes its food seriously and one that doesn''t . restauranteur can take their business to the next level ."},{"type":"p","text":"What are some of your favorite French culinary terms ? Share them with us in the comments below! Until next time, happy cooking! Or as they say in France, bon appetit"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_9f429deb01ed4fafa84df90fd252b4ca~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-09', 'published'),
  ('how-to-increase-customer-retention', 'How to Increase Customer Retention', 'As a business owner, you''re always looking for ways to attract new customers. But what about your current customer base? Are you doing everything you can to keep them coming back?', '[{"type":"p","text":"As a business owner, you''re always looking for ways to attract new customers. But what about your current customer base? Are you doing everything you can to keep them coming back?"},{"type":"p","text":"There are a number of things you can do to turn your one-time customers into loyal, repeat bookings. Here are a few tips:"},{"type":"p","text":"1\\. Get to know your customers. Take the time to learn their names and what they like. This personal touch will make them feel valued and appreciated."},{"type":"p","text":"2\\. Offer discounts or rewards for repeat bookings. This could be something as simple as a 10% discount on their next purchase."},{"type":"p","text":"3\\. Make it easy for them to book again. Have an online booking system set up so they can quickly and easily book their next appointment."},{"type":"p","text":"4\\. Follow up after their visit. Send them a thank you note or give them a call to see how their experience was. This shows that you care about your customers and value their feedback."},{"type":"p","text":"By following these tips, you''ll be on your way to turning your one-time customers into loyal, repeat bookings. And that''s good for business!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_a136d0aee1374cf88a9b832c0c284e2d~mv2.png', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-03', 'published'),
  ('how-to-save-money-when-starting-a-restaurant', 'How to Save Money When Starting a Restaurant?', 'You''re finally ready to take the leap and open a restaurant. However, due to personal financial constraints and the way the market looks right now, you need to start out on a serious budget. Here are some tips on how to...', '[{"type":"p","text":"You''re finally ready to take the leap and open a restaurant. However, due to personal financial constraints and the way the market looks right now, you need to start out on a serious budget. Here are some tips on how to save money when starting a restaurant:"},{"type":"p","text":"1\\. Use technology to your advantage. There are a number of ways that you can use technology to save money when starting a restaurant. For example, you can use online ordering systems to avoid the need to hire extra staff for taking orders. You can also use point-of-sale (POS) systems to streamline your operations and reduce your costs."},{"type":"p","text":"2\\. Start small. One of the best ways to save money when starting a restaurant is to start small. This means avoiding the need to build a large, expensive kitchen and dining area. Instead, focus on creating a smaller, more intimate space that can be easily managed on a tight budget."},{"type":"p","text":"3\\. Avoid unnecessary costs. There are a number of costs associated with starting a restaurant that can be avoided if you''re careful. For example, you may be able to save money by leasing rather than buying equipment. You can also save on costs by using recycled or second-hand materials for your decor."},{"type":"p","text":"4\\. Use coupons and discounts. Another great way to save money when starting a restaurant is to take advantage of coupons and discounts. Many food suppliers offer significant discounts to restaurants that order in bulk. You can also find discounts on kitchen equipment and other supplies by shopping around online."},{"type":"p","text":"5\\. Think outside the traditional restaurant model. If you''re really serious about saving money when starting a restaurant, you may need to think outside the traditional model. For example, consider starting a food truck or pop-up restaurant instead of a brick-and-mortar establishment. These types of businesses often have lower start-up costs and can be just as successful as traditional restaurants."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_a4f9462106f44c4ca96eb9122fef31d0~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2019-01-02', 'published');
